-- wa_northeast_ridge_1963_route: Remove the 'Cascade Pass' waypoint (Junction, 5392 ft, 3.6 mi) from the ascent chain -- this route's own approach text and multiple independent sources (SummitPost, Dr. Dirtbag NE Buttress TR, 'Where is Kyle Miller') confirm the approach descends from near the trailhead (a quarter-mile hike back down the road at a hairpin turn) directly to a Cascade River ford, reaching serious ground at ~3,500 ft within about a half-hour -- it never goes near Cascade Pass (5,392 ft, 3.6 mi up the maintained trail). The row's own approach/approach_variants text corroborates this and never mentions Cascade Pass.
UPDATE routes SET waypoints = '[{"lat": 48.4755, "lng": -121.075, "elev": 3600, "name": "Cascade Pass Trailhead (end of Cascade River Road)", "note": "", "type": "Trailhead", "elevFt": 3600, "directions": "Drive Cascade River Road to its end at the Cascade Pass trailhead, near 3,600 ft. The road is generally open late June through September, and this route''s season is tied to it. This is one of the shortest approaches in the range: the serious ground starts around 3,500 ft, within an hour of the car, so there is no long walk to warm up on."}, {"lat": 48.4655, "lng": -121.079, "elev": 4300, "name": "Cascade River Crossing / Terminal Moraine", "note": "Off-trail descent and ford of the infant Cascade River below the terminal moraine.", "type": "Hazard", "distMi": 4.3}, {"lat": 48.4665, "lng": -121.085, "elev": 5200, "name": "Base of C-J Couloir", "note": "Gain rock just before the Cascade-Johannesburg couloir narrows; the NE Ridge (1963) climbs the rib right of the couloir.", "type": "Junction", "distMi": 4.8}, {"lat": 48.4665, "lng": -121.088, "elev": 6800, "name": "Hanging Glacier Traverse", "note": "Exposed rising traverse beneath Johannesburg''s hanging glaciers; rockfall and icefall hazard.", "type": "Hazard", "distMi": 5.5}, {"lat": 48.46472, "lng": -121.09194, "elev": 8066, "name": "Johannesburg Mountain", "type": "Summit", "elevFt": 8066}]'::jsonb WHERE id = 'wa_northeast_ridge_1963_route';

-- wa_northwest_arete: dist_km corrected from 19.31 to 9.66 -- the stored value (19.31 km = 12.00 mi exactly) matches this row's own round-trip total (waypoint distMi=6 one-way to summit; itinerary day1 6 mi + day2 6 mi = 12 mi round trip), i.e. it stored the already-doubled round-trip figure rather than the one-way value the app's distKm*2 display convention expects. Halved to match the row's own one-way distance.
